<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- The entitlements for an ad-hoc signed build — which is every build until a
	     Developer ID certificate exists. Identical to Steno.entitlements except for
	     the library-validation exception below, which such a build cannot run without.

	     The hardened runtime turns on library validation, and library validation only
	     lets a process load code signed by the same team as itself, or by Apple. Two
	     ad-hoc signatures have no team at all, and are therefore not the same team:
	     dyld refuses to map Sparkle.framework out of the app's own bundle with
	     "mapping process and mapped file (non-platform) have different Team IDs", and
	     the app dies before `main` runs. Ad-hoc plus hardened runtime plus an embedded
	     framework is exactly this project's shape, so this is not an edge case but the
	     default build.

	     The exception is deliberately confined to that build. The release workflow and
	     scripts/release.sh pass Config/Steno.entitlements instead as soon as a
	     Developer ID is available: signed with one certificate, app and framework are
	     the same team, library validation passes on its own, and a shipped app should
	     not carry a weakening entitlement it does not need. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
